re-closing and post-closing acquisition-related earnings charges could adversely impact operating results and cash flows in any given period, and the impact may be substantially different from period to period;","context":"•The inheritance of known, and the discovery of unknown, issues or liabilities;","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":222,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"762ef9bde394bf0dfae5ccb9c78607e8071c2162901f3882b9d2463962b2fead","quote":"•The failure of acquired entities to meet or exceed expected operating results or cash flows could result in impairment of goodwill or intangible assets acquired;","context":"•Pre-closing and post-closing acquisition-related earnings charges could adversely impact operating results and cash flows in any given period, and the impact may be substantially different from period to period;","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":223,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"dda53a2982c88f028a1cd2ce0556fc48eb5e34fc60441471f75230e4e3f28c3c","quote":"•The ability to implement internal controls and accounting systems necessary to be compliant with requirements applicable to public companies subject to SEC reporting, which could result in misstated financial reports; and","context":"•The failure of acquired entities to meet or exceed expected operating results or cash flows could result in impairment of goodwill or intangible assets acquired;","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":224,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"1f389d070e5981c0082b7db50f5490c99eea7d0af0f77e908843385f55e8a90d","quote":"•Future acquisitions could result in changes such as potentially dilutive issuances of equity securities and the incurrence of debt and contingent liabilities.","context":"•The ability to implement internal controls and accounting systems necessary to be compliant with requirements applicable to public companies subject to SEC reporting, which could result in misstated financial reports; and","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":225,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"06f10a399ede70f452ef1a0d2695e028ba2648b9032c83c552e3b970b43451e3","quote":"On September 30, 2025, the Company acquired Elo Holdings, Inc. (“Elo”) for a purchase price of approximately $1.3 billion, a transaction that is significant in size, representing approximately 9% of the Company’s market capitalization on such date. This acquisition substantially increased the Company’s goodwill and other intangible assets, which could become impaired and result in material non-cash charges if we fail to achieve the expected operating results and cash flows. The Company may not be able to successfully integrate Elo's business operations and personnel and to realize the anticipated growth opportunities and cost synergies, and the integration process may divert management's attention from other business priorities. Failure to successfully manage these and other risks associated with this acquisition, including those outlined above, may have a material adverse effect on our business and operating results.","context":"•Future acquisitions could result in changes such as potentially dilutive issuances of equity securities and the incurrence of debt and contingent liabilities.","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":226,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"f966c53c327b8233e5a612a2bd96fc9ae5f0c0c1829f66f4e37a53a25a43b7ab","quote":"The Company may not be able to continue to develop offerings to address user needs effectively. To be successful, we must adapt to rapidly changing technological and application needs by continually improving our offerings, as well as introducing new offerings to address user demands.","context":"On September 30, 2025, the Company acquired Elo Holdings, Inc. (“Elo”) for a purchase price of approximately $1.3 billion, a transaction that is significant in size, representing approximately 9% of the Company’s market capitalization on such date. This acquisition substantially increased the Company’s goodwill and other intangible assets, which could become impaired and result in material non-cash charges if we fail to achieve the expected operating results and cash flows. The Company may not be able to successfully integrate Elo's business operations and personnel and to realize the anticipated growth opportunities and cost synergies, and the integration process may divert management's attention from other business priorities. Failure to successfully manage these and other risks associated with this acquisition, including those outlined above, may have a material adverse effect on our business and operating results.","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":227,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"bbe2147a0143efe64d1662c06610cc85d9d0117c513642d8f52569189a51bbff","quote":"Future success will depend on our ability to effectively and economically adapt in this evolving environment. We could incur substantial costs if we must modify our business to adapt to these changes, and may even be unable to adapt to these changes.","context":"•Changing security protocols.","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":235,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"76715387e4b9cf2223a8a3b76c2caab3d69bb34a4569e235e4c9d7ed7ba07ab3","quote":"The Company participates in a competitive industry, which may become more competitive. Competitors may be able to respond more quickly to new or emerging technology and changes in customer requirements. The markets that we serve are rapidly evolving and highly competitive. Some of our offerings are in direct competition with similar or alternative offerings provided by our competitors. In addition, we often compete with local competitors that may have a substantial advantage in attracting customers in their countries due to more established branding in that country, greater knowledge with respect to the tastes and preferences of customers residing in that country or their focus on a single market. Because of the potential for consolidation in any market, such competitors may become larger, and increased size could permit them to operate in wider geographic areas. To remain competitive, we believe we must continue to effectively and economically:","context":"Future success will depend on our ability to effectively and economically adapt in this evolving environment. We could incur substantial costs if we must modify our business to adapt to these changes, and may even be unable to adapt to these changes.","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":236,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Arch