isruptive technologies and business models;","context":"•Identify and evolve with customer needs, emerging technologies, and industry trends;","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":238,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"231a5dbc18ff25b63c0ded084cfd84cd6a5be9932d14a03fb54471e52fb05052","quote":"•Innovate, develop and timely commercialize new technologies and offerings;","context":"•Monitor disruptive technologies and business models;","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":239,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"c127a759dcc4650ce1e03c92d318533ba9e38f9b4723ecfb615aee3369241960","quote":"•Provide offerings of high quality and reliability;","context":"•Offer superior customer service;","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":244,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"d0bc4fe959f67d5a4867b044744a77ab25137395517ca29847836918cc79e6f6","quote":"•Provide dependable and efficient distribution networks; and","context":"•Provide offerings of high quality and reliability;","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":245,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"d2e2908e6a0547a1c5f595ad5c9c07706d8539f956158138f1c912a030cb6f73","quote":"•Attract, retain and develop employees with technical expertise and an understanding of our industry and customer needs.","context":"•Provide dependable and efficient distribution networks; and","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":246,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"0f5dee720100829d70e6de823e2b4e7f862c379f94cebf969e1e8d008bb259c3","quote":"We cannot assure that we will be able to compete successfully against current or future competitors or technologies. Current or future competitors are likely to continue to develop and introduce new and enhanced offerings that could cause a decline in market acceptance of our offerings, or result in the loss of major customers. Increased competition in our industry may result in price reductions, lower gross profit margins, and loss of market share, and could require increased spending on research and development, sales and marketing, and customer support. In addition, we may not be able to effectively anticipate and react to new entrants in the marketplace competing with our offerings. Further, as we expand into markets beyond our core offerings, we may face well established competitors, placing us at a disadvantage in a new competitive landscape. Some competitors may make strategic acquisitions or establish cooperative relationships with suppliers or companies that produce complementary offerings, which may create additional pressures on our competitive position in the marketplace. An inability to compete successfully could have an adverse effect on our business and results of operations.","context":"•Attract, retain and develop employees with technical expertise and an understanding of our industry and customer needs.","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":247,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"91d3a646bacbcddb770a748b11eb6bf7782789806572070dab0d5be4daad701a","quote":"The Company has substantial operations and sells a significant portion of our offerings outside of the U.S. and purchases important components, including final offerings, from suppliers located outside the U.S., many of whom with operations concentrated in China. Shipments to non-U.S. customers are expected to continue to account for a material portion of Net sales. We also expect to continue the use of third-party contract manufacturing services with non-U.S. production and assembly operations for our offerings.","context":"Operational Risks","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":249,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"d4c8e194da0d5ec3b76a6e38cca31c1aac1ddaa7477e990e46132d78668d7532","quote":"Risks associated with operations, sales, and purchases include:","context":"The Company has substantial operations and sells a significant portion of our offerings outside of the U.S. and purchases important components, including final offerings, from suppliers located outside the U.S., many of whom with operations concentrated in China. Shipments to non-U.S. customers are expected to continue to account for a material portion of Net sales. We also expect to continue the use of third-party contract manufacturing services with non-U.S. production and assembly operations for our offerings.","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":250,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"836c7f7973f79ad2f7572a108873514973c2007c80d5cef5021f9fc7fea29bab","quote":"•Fluctuating foreign currency rates could restrict sales, increase costs of purchasing, and affect collection of receivables outside of the U.S.;","context":"Risks associated with operations, sales, and purchases include:","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":251,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"99bd9c3863bc2c023744069bac083c5fa8ec4b09d48375b86f0338ab27f290db","quote":"•Volatility in foreign credit markets may affect the financial well-being of our customers and suppliers;","context":"•Fluctuating foreign currency rates could restrict sales, increase costs of purchasing, and affect collection of receivables outside of the U.S.;","section":"Item 1A.Risk Factors","block":252,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001628280-26-007668","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-12","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000877212","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877212/000162828026007668/zbra-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c.bin","sha256":"8d5d6fa7c91ec9259b10e03266118cf27e159f32f7fb8ff105a633ea0d302e1c"}},{"id":"ec93b2a806008af91e7c6419ba19ac2000764c254e46df94f132cf3c54e8720d","quote":"•Violations of anti-corruption laws, including the Foreign Corrupt Practices Act and the U.K. Bribery Act,